# Deploy lock (Los Compadres / truck1)

**High priority.** The live website must stay in sync with the committed Cursor workspace.

## Locked targets (never change without explicit user approval)

| Service | Target |
|---------|--------|
| GitHub | remote **`truck1`** → `https://github.com/tacosfernando3-dot/truck1.git` · branch **`main`** |
| Vercel | Team **Los Compadres Taqueria** (`team_B5lEl3kRAYWPFqvq1yeSCnvW`) · project **`truck1`** (`prj_N8vdkZkOQ4JcJF3sT1UhmBfTZFt4`) |
| Live | https://loscompadrestaqueriany.com · https://truck1-los-compadres-taqueria.vercel.app |
| Supabase | `https://pwptpxvhdlscyebbqgkt.supabase.co` |

Do **not** push to `origin` or `odio-dev` (Over Drive). Do **not** deploy to other Vercel teams/projects.

## Ship protocol (required)

After finishing user-facing work, or whenever the user asks to push / deploy / sync / go live:

1. `git status` + `git diff` — commit all intended project changes (never `los-compadres.env` or secrets).
2. `git push truck1 HEAD:main` (not bare `git push`).
3. Confirm via Vercel that a **production** deployment for commit SHA is **READY** and aliased to `loscompadrestaqueriany.com`.
4. If the push already landed but live looks stale: empty-commit or re-push to force a new production deploy; tell the user to hard-refresh.

## Do not leave Cursor ahead of live

- Do not end a session with uncommitted site changes the user expects live, unless they asked to keep them local.
- If local `main` is ahead of `truck1/main`, push before saying the site is updated.
- Local `npm run dev` is not production — production only updates after `truck1` `main` deploys on Vercel.

## Verify commands

```bash
git fetch truck1 && git status -sb
git log -1 --oneline
git push truck1 HEAD:main
```
